A cozy, warmly-lit traditional Chinese kitchen scene in Marc Chagall's dreamlike floating style, featuring an elderly woman with a knowing smile hovering whimsically above a wooden table where a whole fish floats alongside an oversized wok that seems too small. Swirling memories depicted as translucent cooking pans of different sizes spiral upward through the scene. Rich jewel tones of deep reds, golden yellows, and midnight blues dominate. A small window reveals a monkey silhouette against a full moon. Kitchen utensils and herbs drift weightlessly around the composition, suggesting the passage of time and handed-down traditions. The fish appears both whole and sectioned simultaneously, representing the duality of tradition and reason.
